    69	
    70	## Divergences (engine kernel not edited)
    71	
    72	- **D1:** Python `int()` accepts non-ASCII Unicode decimal digit strings
    73	  (`"٣"`, `"３"`). Rust errors on them as PICKUP/PLACE counts
    74	  (probes 057, 058, 090, 091). Rust drops them as BUY_SEED, SELL, BUY_PRODUCT
    75	  and BUY_ANIMAL quantities, while Python executes three units (probes 167, 168,
    76	  204, 205, 241, 242, 278, 279). It was first found in the free-hire edge game
    77	  at step 13: `BUY_PRODUCT FERTILIZER "٣"`, expected money 2,159, Rust 2,460.
    78	- **D2:** Python raises `TypeError` on an unhashable array or object in these
    79	  positions: a unit verb, a PLANT crop (including in a missing hand), a
    80	  PICKUP/PLACE item, or a BUY_SEED/BUY_ANIMAL item. Rust accepts the step as a
    81	  no-op. See probes 030–035, 102–113, 118, 144, 145, 179, 180, 290 and 291.
    82	
    83	Seven repros in `engine_rs/fixtures/generated/divergence-*.jsonl.gz` (minimal
    84	since the verification fixes below) are expected failures. Rust asserts their exact line, step, kind and field.
    85	Evidence is kept in `evidence/first-failing-games/`: the first five failing
    86	full-game traces, with `rust-report.json` giving each first divergence (steps
    87	13, 14, 15, 30 and 45).
