    93	## Verification fixes (verify-1.1b-r1)
    94	
    95	Codex verified `9ee7fb8` (report
    96	`/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-1.1b-r1.md`):
    97	APPROVE WITH EDITS, no blocking findings. Commit `6217868` fixes each edit.
    98	Tests were written before the fixes; the Rust rollback tests (unresolved names)
    99	and the repro manifest test were observed failing first:
   100	
   101	- **Sweep classification.** `classify` matched inputs only, so a trace corrupted
   102	  at `public.day` on a D1 line was reported as D1 with `new_divergences: 0`.
   103	  `confirmed_class` now requires the observed signature: D2 needs a `rejected`
   104	  record, `TypeError: unhashable type` and Rust `rust_accepted`; D1 needs a
   105	  Python-accepted transition and a Rust recheck, with only that line's Unicode
   106	  digits spelled in ASCII, that passes the line. Receipt:
   107	  `verify-r1/negative-classification.log` (the reviewer's corruption,
   108	  `{'unclassified': 1}`, new 1).
   109	- **Null probe.** `None` was the no-script sentinel, so probe 296 (`null` whole
   110	  action) submitted PASS. `scripted_choices` submits scripted actions exactly;
   111	  probe 296 now records `null`, Python accepts it and Rust agrees.
   112	- **Rollback check.** Rejected steps compared order-insensitive `Value`s and
   113	  skipped statuses/rewards/done. `rollback_difference` compares public and
   114	  private values and key order, statuses, rewards and completion; three Rust
   115	  tests cover key-order-only, private-order and scalar mutations.
   116	- **Minimal repros.** The seven divergence fixtures are one-step games
   117	  (`episodeSteps` 2) whose first seat-0 action carries only the divergent
   118	  field; they diverge at line 1, step 0 with the recorded kinds and fields.
   119	  They were regenerated live; the eight game traces are byte-identical. The 15
